{
  "summary": "Analyzed all CLI commands in pipeline.py. The following commands are purely CLI conveniences that duplicate TUI/webui functionality and should be removed: `new` (item creation), `ls` (listing), `review` (interactive agent review session), `design-ref` (set/show design reference), `reject` (reject feature), `restore` (restore rejected feature), `done` (mark feature done), `status` (show feature details), the entire `agent` group (`list`, `use`, `set-model`, `clear-model` — agent config is editable via config.json or webui), and the entire `edit-feature` group (`set-field`, `get-field`, `set-test-results` — all editable from TUI/webui). Commands that MUST be kept: `tui` (launches TUI), `auto` (automation loop used by service), `run` (pipeline execution), `restart` (resume from phase), `service install/uninstall/status` (systemd controls — explicitly requested to keep), `lock status/clear` (operational), all `schedule` subcommands (scheduling infrastructure), all `runs` subcommands (run history), and the helper functions they depend on (`get_config`, `find_feature_or_exit`, `_find_schedule_or_exit`). The `FIELD_SETTERS`, `FIELD_GETTERS`, and `_read_input` helper can also be removed as they only serve `edit-feature`. This cleanup would remove ~400 lines (~30% of the file) and simplify the CLI surface to only automation/operational commands."
}
